# AI DIRECTIVE: SIMPLIFIED TDD WORKFLOW
⚠️ CRITICAL SYSTEM DIRECTIVE ⚠️

Follow this simplified test-driven development workflow for each feature:

1. SELECT a file and feature to work on
   - Identify available feature files in the project
   - Choose the first [to-do] feature you encounter
   - If a feature is [in-progress], prioritize continuing that one
   - Document which file and feature you're working on
   - Update feature status to [in-progress]

2. WRITE simple failing tests
   - Create minimal, focused test cases that verify the expected behavior
   - Keep tests small and specific to the feature
   - Run the tests to confirm they fail (this is important!)
   - Output the test results showing the failure
   - Update feature status to [test-failing]

3. IMPLEMENT simple changes to make tests pass
   - Write only the minimum code needed to pass the tests
   - Focus on functionality first, not optimization
   - Keep changes focused and minimal
   - Document what changes you're making and why
   - Update feature status to [implementing]

4. RUN tests to verify passing
   - Run the tests again to confirm they now pass
   - Output the test results showing success
   - Check that no regressions were introduced
   - Update feature status to [test-passing]

5. PERFORM performance check
   - Run a simple check with typical usage
   - Look for obvious performance issues only
   - No complex benchmarking needed
   - Document any observations
   - Update feature status to [performance-verified]

6. UPDATE feature status to [done]
   - Mark the feature as complete in its file
   - Summarize what was implemented
   - Document any notes for future reference

7. REPEAT process with next feature
   - Return to step 1 for the next [to-do] feature
   - Maintain this cycle for continuous progress

Status Types:
- [to-do]: Not started
- [in-progress]: Being worked on
- [test-failing]: Tests written but failing
- [implementing]: Code being written
- [test-passing]: Tests now passing
- [performance-verified]: Performance checked
- [done]: Feature complete

Important Guidelines:
- Complete each step fully before moving to the next
- Document your progress at each step
- Keep changes small and focused
- Prioritize completing one feature before starting another
- If unsure which feature to work on, ask for clarification
- Always verify tests fail before implementation
- Always verify tests pass after implementation

This workflow ensures systematic, test-driven development of features with clear status tracking.
